			{"id":"d-truques-desafio-t","type":"text","x":3055,"y":2950,"width":550,"height":60,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"frameId":"l-truques","text":"Challenge: lock the vase with ⌘⇧L and try to drag it.","originalText":"Challenge: lock the vase with ⌘⇧L and try to drag it.","fontSize":24,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"center","verticalAlign":"middle","containerId":"d-truques-desafio","lineHeight":1.25},
			{"id":"d-relacoes-titulo","type":"text","x":40,"y":3336,"width":290.4,"height":55,"strokeColor":"#c2255c","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"frameId":"l-relacoes","text":"🏷️ Relations","originalText":"🏷️ Relations","fontSize":44,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","lineHeight":1.25},
			{"id":"d-relacoes-texto","type":"text","x":40,"y":3420,"width":580,"height":421.2,"strokeColor":"#343a40","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"frameId":"l-relacoes","text":"An arrow between two notes can become a relation:\n1. Connect the two notes with the Arrow.\n2. With the arrow selected, click Promote to relation, at the top right.\n3. Give the relation a name, like inspires or depends_on.\n4. Verso shows the change at the top of the note the arrow leaves from and writes it when you confirm.\nThe relation becomes a link in the note: it shows in the other one's backlinks and follows renames.","originalText":"An arrow between two notes can become a relation:\n1. Connect the two notes with the Arrow.\n2. With the arrow selected, click Promote to relation, at the top right.\n3. Give the relation a name, like inspires or depends_on.\n4. Verso shows the change at the top of the note the arrow leaves from and writes it when you confirm.\nThe relation becomes a link in the note: it shows in the other one's backlinks and follows renames.","fontSize":24,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","lineHeight":1.35,"autoResize":false},
			{
				"id":"d-relacoes-desafio",
				"type":"rectangle",
				"x":40,
				"y":4000,
				"width":580,
				"height":160,
				"strokeColor":"#f08c00",
				"backgroundColor":"#ffec99",
				"fillStyle":"solid",
				"strokeWidth":1,
				"strokeStyle":"solid",
				"roughness":1,
				"opacity":100,
				"roundness":{"type":3},
				"frameId":"l-relacoes",
				"boundElements":[
					{"id":"d-relacoes-desafio-t","type":"text"}
				]
			},
			{"id":"d-relacoes-desafio-t","type":"text","x":55,"y":4020,"width":550,"height":120,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"frameId":"l-relacoes","text":"Challenge: connect Project Alpha to Project Beta, promote the arrow to “inspires” and open Project Alpha to see the new property.","originalText":"Challenge: connect Project Alpha to Project Beta, promote the arrow to “inspires” and open Project Alpha to see the new property.","fontSize":24,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"center","verticalAlign":"middle","containerId":"d-relacoes-desafio","lineHeight":1.25},
			{"id":"d-buscar-titulo","type":"text","x":1540,"y":3336,"width":459.8,"height":55,"strokeColor":"#0c8599","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"frameId":"l-buscar","text":"🔎 Search and export","originalText":"🔎 Search and export","fontSize":44,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","lineHeight":1.25},
			{"id":"d-buscar-texto","type":"text","x":1540,"y":3420,"width":580,"height":324,"strokeColor":"#343a40","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"frameId":"l-buscar","text":"• • Search the board (⌘F) finds cards, the notes' text and the drawn texts, ignoring accents; Enter goes to the next.\n• The Outline lists groups, cards and connections; Include the drawing's annotations shows the drawn texts too.\n• Export image (⌘⇧E): PNG or SVG, from 1× to 3×, with or without background, light or dark, the whole board or Selection only — and then Save in the folder, Save to Downloads or Copy.","originalText":"• • Search the board (⌘F) finds cards, the notes' text and the drawn texts, ignoring accents; Enter goes to the next.\n• The Outline lists groups, cards and connections; Include the drawing's annotations shows the drawn texts too.\n• Export image (⌘⇧E): PNG or SVG, from 1× to 3×, with or without background, light or dark, the whole board or Selection only — and then Save in the folder, Save to Downloads or Copy.","fontSize":24,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","lineHeight":1.35,"autoResize":false},
			{
				"id":"d-buscar-desafio",
				"type":"rectangle",
				"x":1540,
				"y":4000,
